WEBVTT

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.460
This place is no good either.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.430
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:01.550
<b>"Love for Lost Sheep"</b>

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.480
Yeah, Isago here.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:10.660
Hayashi-san!

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:11.730
Chief Editor!

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:12.980
Thank you for your hard work.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.270
How is it?

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:17.020
Have you found a shop that you 
think you could do an article on?

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:18.490
W-Well...

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.130
Not a single one.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.080
<i>Get a grip, please, Isago-san.</i>

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:27.450
You finally got this series 
going after so many flops.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.450
<b>Series

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.580
<i>I-I know!</i>

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.140
<i>That's why I'm so tense.</i>

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.840
Here.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.470
<i>All right.</i>

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.930
<i>I'm looking forward to something good.</i>

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.040
<i>Good luck.</i>

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:43.580
<i>The editorial department is full of women.</i>

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.970
<i>They've been pushing me around,</i>

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.980
<i>but my series finally got a green light.</i>

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.730
<i>I'm going to write a good 
article, even if it kills me.</i>

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:55.610
<i>But...</i>

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:01.860
<i>I never knew it could be so hard for a dude 
to go into a fancy café all by himself.</i>

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.120
No way, that's so creepy.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.970
I know, right? I mean, seriously?

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:09.010
Did someone just call me creepy?

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:16.010
Yeah, it's just not right for a guy 
to come into a shop like this alone.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:18.460
This sucks, but I'm going to have to 
find an easier place to go into...

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.180
Welcome.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.590
That person just now...

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.810
Here you are.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.410
<i>W-Wow!</i>

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.910
<i>He went into a shop full 
of women by himself!</i>

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.270
<i>And he ordered so much!</i>

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.440
<i>Everyone's totally looking at him!</i>

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.610
<i>And yet...</i>

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.040
<i>He's a hero.</i>

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.770
<i>You coward!</i>

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.070
<i>If only I had the heart of that hero...</i>

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.560
<i>That one's no good, either.</i>

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:16.610
I spent a whole week, and every 
single one's been a no-go.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:22.170
It was never possible for an old guy 
to have café sweets by himself.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.710
The article draft's due soon.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:29.490
Maybe I should ask for a 
different series while I can.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:34.580
Maybe I'll challenge myself 
to a "cappuccinos" today.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.750
I hear the cherry tarts are 
the cake of the season.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.590
How gorgeous.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.510
<i>There's a flock of seniors going in!</i>

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.650
<i>A café?</i>

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.890
Today's Specials
Cake of the Season
Strawberry Tarts
 Dessert sets also available
350 yen

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.390
<i>But it doesn't look like one.</i>

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.230
Sorry.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.080
Watch where you're going.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.330
Sorry about that.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.900
Oh, um...

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.110
<i>It just looks like an 
old-school kanmidokoro.</i>

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:08.560
<i>No, come to think of it, kanmidokoros 
are the Japanese equivalent of a café.</i>

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.120
<i>Considering the customers 
that just went in...</i>

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.880
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.250
Welcome.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:24.990
Right this way.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.180
<i>This place seems nostalgic.</i>

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.470
<i>It's comforting how it's not </i>too<i> fancy.</i>

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:37.440
<i>And...</i>

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.690
<i>They have so many sweets on the menu!</i>

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:50.430
<i>Oh yeah, those seniors and those punks...</i>

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.930
The parfaits here are the best.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:56.040
I know.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.420
<i>Th-They fit right in!</i>

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:03.230
I heard they're doing a rerun of 
<i>Ohoka Sabaki</i> starting next week.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:05.920
I'll have to record that.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.150
Your latte art is as good as ever, boss.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.050
I tried a cat today.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:13.560
One cappuccino.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:17.320
<i>The customers are diverse,</i>

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:20.730
<i>but you can tell everyone's here 
because they like it here.</i>

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.280
<i>This is great.</i>

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:25.570
Here you are.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.960
Matcha and seasonal raw sweets.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:30.200
Mini-anmitsu and three kinds of dango.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:34.660
<i>Here we go! Café sweets for a single man!</i>

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.350
Thank y—

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:41.880
You're...

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.510
You're that hero!

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:46.880
No...

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.170
You're that good man!

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.180
Sorry about earlier.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:07:01.650
My name is Isago. I'm a reporter for 
a community magazine called <i>G! Moto</i>.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:02.710
A reporter.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:04.440
Oh, I've read it before.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:09.570
I'm going around to various 
cafés for a new series.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.210
Man, this is a great shop.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.470
I couldn't help but make myself at home.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.770
Thank you.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:17.290
Umm...

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:20.520
So you're reporting on cafés, right?

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:21.080
Yes.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:25.540
Then why did you leave 
without entering that shop?

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:30.980
Judging from how you ate here, 
you must love sweets, don't you?

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.340
Well...

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.460
I couldn't bring myself to go in.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.350
But why?

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.600
I don't have the guts.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:46.420
All the popular shops are full of women.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:49.740
It's just not the kind of place that an old 
guy like me could just walk in by himself.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.570
It's true that they have 
a lot of female customers,

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.120
but you don't need to let that get to you.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:08:00.620
Indeed, you walked in 
without a single thought.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.390
And you ordered a ton of 
cake and started eating it

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:04.880
without even noticing all 
the eyes that were on you!

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:09.580
Oh, so that's why he's a hero.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:13.830
That's why his hobby is desserts 
and known for his swee—

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:15.590
Shut up!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.850
Oh no, the hero is using violence.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.160
But...

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.710
I don't have such courage.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:27.120
I was never fit to write 
about cutting-edge cafés.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.820
I'm in over my head.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:33.320
It was never something I could do.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.320
I'll come up with something 
that's more my speed.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:39.830
I know.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:46.180
You just need Tsubaki-kun to pass on 
the secrets of the Café-for-One.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:47.340
What?

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.020
I mean, you're a pro.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.050
A pro what?!

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:52.180
That's a great idea.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.810
Sui, you, too?

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:56.160
We have tomorrow off.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.550
Why don't you go tour some 
cafés, Tsubaki-kun?

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:03.680
You would feel more comfortable if you had 
Tsubaki-kun along with you, wouldn't you?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.440
Yes, of course.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:13.190
Could you please?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:20.670
Well, just for one day, I guess.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:26.370
Sorry I dragged you out in 
the spur of the moment.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.540
I'm taking up your day off.

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:30.100
It's fine.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:31.500
I do it all the time anyway.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:34.800
You wanted to go to HARU Café today, right?

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:36.060
Yes.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:38.800
I've always wanted to try 
the fruit waffles there.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:42.600
They do have big portions. 
They're photogenic.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.150
I heard they started making French toast, 
too, which turned out to be a hit.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.130
I knew I could count on 
the Café-for-One pro.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.050
I'm not a pro.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.210
There it is.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.870
I-I feel like we're drawing even more 
attention, just two dudes here...

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.450
May I take your order?

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:12.390
Cream cheese and berry 
waffles and blend coffee.

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:13.280
Okay.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:14.340
What about you?

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:15.800
Umm...

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.310
A café au lait and...

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:20.430
A sandwich?

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:21.600
Denied.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.560
Isago-san, you're here for the 
fruit waffles, aren't you?

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.850
But I mean, maybe it's weird 
for a geezer like me.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.660
That's wrong.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:32.860
Buy the waffles.

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:36.980
A café au lait and fruit waffles, please.

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:38.340
Understood.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.490
I-I've dreamt of this...

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:50.920
The fruit waffles!

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.010
<i>A-All right, me, too.</i>

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.710
I-It's so...

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:10.520
It has a crisp surface and 
a firm dough on the inside,

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:13.780
with sweet strawberry sauce 
and hand-made gelato.

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:17.320
And with the fluffy cream 
on top, it's just...

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.430
The best!

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:29.830
S-Sorry, I'm getting a bit too excited.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:31.760
I think it's fine.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:35.170
Just be who you are, the way you are now.

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:39.160
Everyone has their own way 
of spending time in a café.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:46.160
<i>Oh, yeah, I thought people 
would stare at us more, but...</i>

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.760
Everyone eat and drinks what they like.

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.020
You're free to spend the time as you like.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:53.770
As you like?

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:54.820
Yes.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:58.780
Were you thinking about the people around 
you while you were eating your waffles?

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:01.370
See?

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.310
There isn't much

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.160
to a café.

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.430
I see.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.890
You're as wise as always, Tsubaki-kun.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.000
Heyo.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.540
Wh-Why?!

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:23.010
It's the fate of a café to create 
such coincidences, perhaps.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.550
You're just talking out of your ass!

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:29.570
Tsubaki-kun's shy around new people, so we 
wanted to make sure he was doing all right.

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:31.560
The waffles are so good.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:34.390
You could have told me you were here.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:38.810
You really don't notice.

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:41.270
I feel stupid for having been 
worried about what people thought.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:42.570
Nah, actually...

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.870
We were careful not to get noticed.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.740
What the hell are you doing in a café?!

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:56.630
Do you think you'll crack the 
secrets of the Café-for-One?

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:57.590
Yes.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:59.130
Thanks to Tsubaki-san.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:04.130
I think I've realized that I don't need to 
stress out about being in over my head.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:05.350
That's it.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:07.550
Just relax and have fun.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:10.060
Be who you are. That's the best.

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:13.810
Oh, and there's something 
I'd like to discuss.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:15.230
Yes?

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:20.330
Could I feature Rokuhoudou as the 
first subject of the new series?

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:24.430
I don't think you could call our 
place a cutting-edge fancy café.

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:25.240
It's fine.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:30.490
I <i>just</i> came up with a great idea.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:39.740
Congrats, Isago-san.

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.000
Your new series is really popular.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.630
Hayashi-san...

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:44.600
Chief Editor.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:47.920
Honestly, I was really worried when you 
said you wanted to start a new series

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.760
right before the deadline.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:53.270
Sorry to worry you.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.580
But thanks to that, I came to a realization.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.220
I don't need to get in over my head.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:00.650
I can just write articles about what 
I can see at my own eye-level.

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:03.410
That's what's important.

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:05.530
Isago-san...

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:06.540
Yes?

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:10.320
Do you have something to share?

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:13.860
You have a different vibe.

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:16.470
You seem like you've grown a little.

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:22.800
Do you think so?

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.120
Oh, hello.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:35.020
<i>If that's true, I know why.</i>

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:39.020
<b>Daddy-o's Café Go!</b>

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:44.020
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.860
Damn it, the weather forecast lied!

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:53.910
This is just the worst timing.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:58.130
I can't find a convenience store, either.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.540
If only there were a place 
I could wait out the rain.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.290
<i>A cat?</i>

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:10.540
<i>In this rain?</i>

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:22.310
A shop? Here?

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:37.330
Um, pardon me...

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:46.490
There's no one here.

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:50.840
I'm a mess.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:56.140
I'm all dressed up, but this is no good.

00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:57.850
Welcome.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.360
So bright.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:10.280
We've been waiting for you.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.040
Miss.

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:25.270
I'm sorry, I'll wipe myself off.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.460
Not to worry, miss.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.470
Could you please close your eyes?

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:36.510
O-O-Okay.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:40.380
Un...

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:44.850
<i>The towel's so fluffy.</i>

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:46.530
Deux...

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.440
<i>A warm wind.</i>

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:53.810
Trois.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.940
<i>I smell flowers.</i>

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:58.540
<i>My whole body's covered in a pleasant scent.</i>

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.930
<i>There's a southern breeze 
from out of nowhere.</i>

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:07.000
<i>This must be paradise.</i>

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:12.050
Miss, open your eyes, please.

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:20.060
A menu for our customer.

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:22.060
Garçon.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:23.410
Oui, Monsieur.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.740
Bonjour!

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.370
Here you are.

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:33.830
Th-Thank you.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.980
<i>This is a menu?</i>

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:38.450
<i>It's so fancy, I can't read it.</i>

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:42.200
I'm sorry, I can't read French.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:44.660
Non, not to worry.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.210
The menu is but a formality.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:54.860
I'll choose for you the perfect 
dish of amore for your heart.

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:57.090
For my heart?

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:02.050
Miss, you have important 
business today, correct?

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:03.440
Y-Yes.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:04.480
But why...

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:09.060
Alas, this sudden rain.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.210
You're freezing, both in body and spirit.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:13.810
Your legs are about to stop.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:15.490
Well...

00:18:15.810 --> 00:18:20.380
I'm still not fully confident, 
especially looking the way I do.

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:23.990
I keep thinking, "What if I make the 
proposal only to get rejected?"

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.120
Understood.

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:29.580
The perfect menu for you...

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:31.620
Chef!

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:33.130
Oui, Monsieur.

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:34.920
Pâtisserie!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:35.840
Oui, Monsieur.

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:40.060
Formation Omega!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.220
Here you are.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.920
The surface of a lake after a rain.

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:27.890
Surface d'un lac.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:33.060
<i>I-I have no idea how they made this 
soup with that process just now...</i>

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:34.980
But thank you.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.720
<i>Wh-What...</i>

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:49.810
<i>The slightly thick soup passes 
gently down the throat.</i>

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:54.090
<i>It's like a blessing rain on dry land.</i>

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:59.460
<i>It fills my body with warmth.</i>

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:04.000
<i>I can feel every cell in 
my body being invigorated.</i>

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:08.020
<i>I feel like my mind can be reborn.</i>

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.590
Did you enjoy it?

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.420
Yes, of course.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.530
Then this flower is for you.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:23.250
Please have confidence.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:27.230
Persian buttercup.

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:29.540
Its flower word meaning is

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:32.200
"You are charming."

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:41.170
I'm going to do this.

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:44.740
Good luck.

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:52.590
Huh?

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:53.940
I was just...

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:56.110
at that shop...

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.570
Was I dreaming?

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:01.770
No way.

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:08.180
<i>We've prepared a modest gift for you.</i>

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.120
<i>Please look up at the sky.</i>

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:23.240
A rainbow...

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:29.370
Am I daydreaming?

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:32.610
I feel like I've been 
spirited away by foxes.

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:36.170
All right.

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:40.690
I'm going to make Daddy-o's 
Café Go Part 2 a smash!

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:30.140
<b>"It Begins with Omurice"</b>

